  "notes": "{進水|しんすい} literally means \"advancing into the water\" ({進|しん} advance + {水|すい} water); it names the specific moment a completed hull first touches the water, distinct from the ship later entering full service.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {進水|しんすい}{式|しき}: launching ceremony\n- {進水|しんすい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to be launched\n- {進水|しんすい}{台|だい}: launching slipway",
